@node Types
@section Types for Mars
@nodedescription Types for working with Mars time.

@c AI disclosure: searched up which commands to use
@deftp {Data type} mars_time_t
Represents the number of Martian seconds since approximately 12:00 UTC,
December 29th 1873, or Virgo 25th 140. When using, be aware that
mars_time_t should not be confused with time_t. Early values of
mars_time_t will represent negative time_t values as it predates the
Unix Epoch.
@end deftp

@deftypevr {Struct} struct mars_tm
The **mars_tm** structure is similar to the **tm** structure, which
represents "broken-down" time.
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_sec
Martian seconds, 0-59
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_min
Minutes, 0-59
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_hour
Hours, 0-23
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_msol
Sol of month, 1-28
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_mon
Month, 0-23
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_year
Year, starting from Darian Calendar Year 0
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_wsol
Sol of week, 0-6
@end deftypevar
@deftypevar {int} mars_tm_ysol
Sol of year, 0-668
@end deftypevar

@end deftypevr

@node Numerical time functions
@section Numerical time functions for Mars
@nodedescription TODO

@c surely there's a better way to do this
@defun ammarstime (mars_time_t* @var{timer})
Analagous to gmtime. Returns a broken down time structure
(struct mars_tm) representing the amount of time since the time stored
in @var{TIMER}.

WARNING: Probably due to float modulus operations, there appears
to be usually 1-2, but sometimes up to 4 seconds of variance in
conversions. This is being investigated.
@end defun

@defun diffmarstime (mars_time_t @var{time_end}, mars_time_t @var{time_start})
Returns the amount of time since time_end and time_start.

It is literally basic subtraction.

This function exists for the sake of matching "standards" because the
difftime function exists.
@end defun

@defun localmarstime (mars_time_t* @var{timer})
The same as ammarstime, except returns the time relative to the
timezone.

NOTE: Timezones are currently unimplemented. This returns MTC for now.
@end defun

@defun mars_time (mars_time_t* @var{timer})
Returns the current value of time elapsed in Martian seconds since MSD
0, and sets @var{timer} to that value if not NULL.
@end defun

@defun mkmarstime (struct mars_tm* @var{tm})
Returns the number of Martian Seconds (mars_time) given the broken down
time structure in @var{tm}.

If @var{tm} is NULL, -1 is returned.
@end defun

