@node Conversion functions
@section Conversion functions
@strong {WARNING: Still a work in progress.}

These are functions that can be used to convert between timekeeping
systems.

@strong {THESE NAMES ARE ESPECIALLY SUBJECT TO CHANGE!}

@defun earth_time_to_msd(time_t @var{et})
Calculates the MSD (Mars Sol Date) given the amount of seconds since
the Unix Epoch (@var{et}).

If programming in C, use of this function is discouraged. It is for use
in a Python binding for libspacetime to match the behavior of Python's
time function, which returns time as a floating point number instead of
an integer.
@end defun

@defun earth_time_to_mars_time(time_t @var{et})
Converts Earth Time (@var{et}) to Martian Time, represented
in seconds since MSD 0.
@end defun

@defun mars_time_to_earth_time(mars_time_t @var{mars_time})
Converts Martian Time (@var{mars_time}) to Earth Time, represented
in seconds since the Unix Epoch.
@end defun
